-- title:
--   Increment of the truncated Petersson pairing across a height shell
-- statement:
--   Let $F$ be a number field, write $G=\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_F)$ for the adelic general linear group of rank $2$ with its Haar measure, $\|\cdot\|$ for the idelic norm (the value of the distributive Haar character), and $H$ for the adelic height. Fix reals $\alpha,\beta$ with $\alpha>0$, reals $c,u,d_1,d_2$ with $c>0$, a compact set $T_c\subseteq G$, and a set $\Phi_0\subseteq G$ such that: $\Phi_0$ lies in the union over $y\in T_c$ of the right translates by $y$ of the centre-cut Siegel set with data $c,u,d_1,d_2$ (those $g$ whose finite part lies in the integral subgroup, with $c\le$ the local height, $x$-window square $\le u^2$ and archimedean determinant norm in $[d_1,d_2]$ at every infinite place); $\Phi_0\subseteq\{g:\|\det g\|\in[\alpha,\beta]\}$; and $\Phi_0$ is a fundamental domain for the left action of the image of $\mathrm{GL}_2(F)$ on $G$ with respect to Haar measure restricted to that determinant slab. Then there exists $R_1\in\mathbb{R}$ with the following property. Let $\nu$ be the additive Haar measure of $\mathbb{A}_F$ conditioned on the adelic box, let $\varphi_N(g)=\int\varphi(n(x)g)\,d\nu(x)$ with $n(x)=\begin{pmatrix}1&x\\0&1\end{pmatrix}$, and $\Lambda_R\varphi=\varphi-\mathbf 1_{\{H>e^R\}}\varphi_N$. For all continuous $E,E':G\to\mathbb{C}$ that are invariant under left multiplication by $\mathrm{GL}_2(F)$, if $\|\Lambda_{R_1}E\|^2$ and $\|\Lambda_{R_1}E'\|^2$ are integrable on $\Phi_0$, then for all $R,R'$ with $R_1\le R\le R'$ the difference of the Petersson pairings at exponent $s=0$, $\int_{\Phi_0}\Lambda_{R'}E\,\overline{\Lambda_{R'}E'}-\int_{\Phi_0}\Lambda_{R}E\,\overline{\Lambda_{R}E'}$, equals the integral over the quotient of $G$ by the subgroup generated by the rational torus and the adelic unipotent subgroup, with respect to the associated quotient measure, of the product of the indicator of the determinant slab at a chosen representative $q$, the indicator of $(e^R,e^{R'}]$ evaluated at $H(q)$, and $E_N(q)\overline{E'_N(q)}$.
--
--   This is the Maass–Selberg style increment identity for the one-cusp truncation operator on $\mathrm{GL}_2$ over a number field: moving the truncation height from $e^R$ to $e^{R'}$ changes the truncated Petersson pairing over a determinant-slab fundamental domain exactly by the pairing of the constant terms over the corresponding height shell. It feeds the two slab-level statements assembling the Maass–Selberg relations for truncated pseudo-Eisenstein series.
